# Repository Context

## This Repository (app-pro-ui)
Main Next.js application for the SEO platform.

## Related Repositories

### pattern-library
- **Purpose**: Shared component library and design system based on Material UI
- **Usage**: Import components from this repo for all UI elements
- **Rule**: Use pattern-library components only, no custom CSS/inline styles
- **Description**: A component library and set of established patterns to guide engineers in building consistent customer tools

### app-api
- **Purpose**: Frontend API for Application Engineering
- **Usage**: Backend API services and data layer
- **Description**: The main API service that provides data and business logic for frontend applications
- **Tech Stack**: Node.js, TypeScript, Pylon framework

### maui
- **Purpose**: Moz Pro unified UI framework (legacy)
- **Usage**: Legacy UI components and patterns (being phased out)
- **Description**: The previous unified UI framework for Moz Pro, now being replaced by app-pro-ui
- **Tech Stack**: React, Material UI v4, Webpack

### moz-ui
- **Purpose**: Next.js powered frontend for Moz account management (sister app to app-pro-ui)
- **Usage**: Account settings, checkout, subscriptions, billing
- **Description**: The Next.js frontend for Moz account management and billing features
- **Tech Stack**: Next.js, React 18, TypeScript
- **Relationship**: Sister application to app-pro-ui - maintain consistency in patterns, tools, and updates

## Integration Guidelines
- Always reference pattern-library for UI components
- Use app-api for backend data services
- Follow established naming conventions across repos
- Maintain consistency with shared design tokens
- Coordinate patterns, tools, and updates between app-pro-ui and moz-ui
- Consider cross-app consistency when making architectural decisions